## Learning goals

This project is designed to connect mathematical notation with concrete Python
code: how shapes constrain operations, how row-major storage affects access
patterns, and how different views of matrix multiplication can produce the same
result. It also provides a small base for comparing the Python implementation
with the planned C++ version.

